dx clean - prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs; use `bazel clean` for those (check by default; --apply prunes; no scopes)

prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs; use `bazel clean` for those (check by default; --apply prunes; no scopes)

Usage: dx clean [--check] [--apply] [--prune-unobserved]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

  -q, --quiet[=<QUIET>]
          Hide summaries. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -v, --verbose[=<VERBOSE>]
          Show more logs. =false turns off an inherited default
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format

      --bazel-startup-option <TOKEN>
          Pass one Bazel startup option (repeatable)

      --check
          Check without changing files

      --apply
          Authorize the managed mutation or effect

      --prune-unobserved
          Prune generations process observation cannot see

  -h, --help
          Print help

Per-command flags: --check (report prune candidates without deleting; default). --apply (authorizes pruning managed state). Never touches Bazel outputs; --output text|json only, diff has no patch. --prune-unobserved (prune generations no process observation protects; without it, unavailable observation preserves unobserved state instead of assuming it idle; never overrides a held lease).

Scopes: none (clean takes no scopes).
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|json; --report has no standard format for this command.
Environment: NO_COLOR=<any> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

